05dzikowo \u2013 Puck \u2013 Swarzewo \u2013 Gnie\u017cd\u017cewo \u2013 \u0141ebcz \u2013 Starzy\u0144ski Dw\u00f3r \u2013 Radoszewo \u2013 Starzyno \u2013 K\u0142anino \u2013 Sulicice \u2013 S\u0142awoszyno \u2013 S\u0142awoszynko \u2013 Karwie\u0144skie B\u0142oto Pierwsze \u2013 Karwie\u0144skie B\u0142oto Drugie \u2013 D\u0119bki \u2013 Bia\u0142og\u00f3ra \u2013 Lubiatowo \u2013 Kopalino \u2013 Osetnik/Stilo \u2013 Sasino \u2013 Ulinia \u2013 Sarbsk \u2013 Now\u0119cin \u2013 \u0141eba \u2013 \u017barnowska \u2013 Ga\u0107 \u2013 Izbica \u2013 Rzuski Las \u2013 Ciemino \u2013 G\u0142\u00f3wczyce \u2013 Sk\u00f3rzyno \u2013 R\u00f3wno \u2013 Rumsko \u2013 Wierzchocino \u2013 \u017belazo \u2013 Smo\u0142dzino \u2013 Gardna Wielka \u2013 Gardna Ma\u0142a \u2013 Retowo \u2013 Rowy.\nWestern section: Rowy \u2013 D\u0119bina \u2013 Podd\u0105bie \u2013 Wytowno \u2013 Orzechowo \u2013 Ustka \u2013 Duninowo \u2013 Zaleskie \u2013 Z\u0142akowo \u2013 Marszewo \u2013 Kr\u00f3lewo \u2013 Korlino \u2013 \u0141\u0105cko \u2013 Jezierzany \u2013 Jaros\u0142awiec \u2013 Wicie \u2013 Dar\u0142owo \u2013 \u017bukowo Morskie \u2013 Bobolin \u2013 D\u0105bki \u2013 Bukowo Morskie \u2013 Gle\u017anowo \u2013 Bielkowo \u2013 Wierciszewo \u2013 Iwi\u0119cino \u2013 Rzepkowo \u2013 Osieki \u2013 \u0141azy \u2013 Unie\u015bcie \u2013 Mielno \u2013 Mielenko \u2013 Ch\u0142opy \u2013 Sarbinowo \u2013 G\u0105ski \u2013 Ple\u015bna \u2013 Ustronie Morskie \u2013 Siano\u017c\u0119ty \u2013 Ko\u0142obrzeg \u2013 Grzybowo \u2013 D\u017awirzyno \u2013 Rogowo \u2013 Mrze\u017cyno \u2013 Pogorzelica \u2013 Niechorze \u2013 Rewal \u2013 Trz\u0119sacz \u2013 Pustkowo \u2013 Pobierowo \u2013 \u0141uk\u0119cin \u2013 Radawka \u2013 Dziwn\u00f3wek \u2013 Dziwn\u00f3w \u2013 Mi\u0119dzywodzie \u2013 \u015awi\u0119tou\u015b\u0107 \u2013 Ko\u0142czewo \u2013 Wise\u0142ka \u2013 Warnowo \u2013 Mi\u0119dzyzdroje \u2013 \u0141unowo \u2013 Warsz\u00f3w \u2013 \u015awinouj\u015bcie.\nGermany.\n&lt;mapframe latitude=\"54.4\" longitude=\"12.0\" zoom=\"5\" height=\"420\" width=\"700\" align=\"center\" text=\"EV10 in Germany \u2014 national section highlighted\" show=\"evbase,evgermany\" /&gt;\nHighlight: \u2501\u2501 German section \u00b7 \u2501\u2501 other mapped EV10 sections.\nAhlbeck \u2013 Heringsdorf \u2013 Bansin \u2013 \u00dcckeritz \u2013 Koserow \u2013 Zinnowitz \u2013 Trassenheide \u2013 Wolgast \u2013 Kr\u00f6slin \u2013 Freest \u2013 Lubmin \u2013 Greifswald \u2013 Stralsund \u2013 R\u00fcgen: Altef\u00e4hr \u2013 Garz \u2013 Putbus \u2013 G\u00f6hren \u2013 Baabe \u2013 Sellin \u2013 Binz \u2013 Sassnitz \u2013 Lohme \u2013 Glowe \u2013 Juliusruh \u2013 Putgarten/Cape Arkona \u2013 Dranske \u2013 Wiek \u2013 Schaprode \u2013 Gingst \u2013 Rambin \u2013 Altef\u00e4hr \u2013 Stralsund \u2013 Barth \u2013 Zingst \u2013 Prerow \u2013 Ahrenshoop \u2013 Wustrow \u2013 Graal-M\u00fcritz \u2013 Warnem\u00fcnde/Rostock \u2013 Wismar \u2013 Travem\u00fcnde \u2013 Neustadt in Holstein \u2013 Gro\u00dfenbrode \u2013 Puttgarden \u2013 Gro\u00dfenbrode \u2013 Oldenburg in Holstein \u2013 Sch\u00f6nberger Strand \u2013 Kiel \u2013 Eckernf\u00f6rde \u2013 Kappeln \u2013 Flensburg/Padborg.\nDenmark.\n&lt;mapframe latitude=\"55.8\" longitude=\"11.3\" zoom=\"6\" height=\"420\" width=\"700\" align=\"center\" text=\"EV10 in Denmark \u2014 national section highlighted\" show=\"evbase,evdenmark\" /&gt;\nHighlight: \u2501\u2501 Danish section \u00b7 \u2501\u2501 other mapped EV10 sections.\nPadborg \u2013 S\u00f8nderborg \u2013 Fynshav \u2013 ferry to S\u00f8by \u2013 \u00c6r\u00f8sk\u00f8bing \u2013 ferry to Svendborg \u2013 Langeland \u2013 Spodsbjerg\u2013T\u00e5rs ferry \u2013 Nakskov \u2013 R\u00f8dbyhavn \u2013 Maribo \u2013 Nyk\u00f8bing Falster \u2013 Stubbek\u00f8bing \u2013 Bog\u00f8 \u2013 M\u00f8ns Klint \u2013 Stege \u2013 R\u00f8dvig \u2013 K\u00f8ge \u2013 Copenhagen.\nTen-day plan for the Polish section.\nThis plan assumes an average touring pace, although two days are long. Consider adding a rest day in Gda\u0144sk or \u0141eba.\nFacilities along the route.\nAccommodation and food.\nThe southern Baltic coast has a dense range of campsites, hostels, guesthouses, apartments and hotels. In high season, lack of vacancies and high prices are a greater issue than a lack of properties. In northern Sweden and Finland, the spacing of accommodation may dictate a longer or shorter day, unless you are prepared to camp wild.\nIn Sweden and Finland, the right to access can be used, but camping is restricted in national parks, nature reserves, near homes and on cultivated land. Campsites, shelters and designated primitive camps are popular in Denmark. In Poland, Germany and the Baltic states, use legal campsites or obtain the landowner's permission.\nFood and supplies are easy to find in Denmark, Germany, Poland and southern Sweden. On the Estonian islands, in Courland and along the northern coasts of Sweden and Finland, check shop hours and carry enough supplies for the following day.\nOne-way Copenhagen\u2013Gda\u0144sk bicycle rental.\nSince 2026, a bicycle can be rented near Copenhagen and returned in Gda\u0144sk, or ridden in the opposite direction, without returning it to the original rental location. The service was developed by the Danish company OneWayBikeTours and the Gda\u0144sk tour operator Poland by Locals as part of Baltic Biking UPGRADE. EuroVelo has a description of the launch.\nPick-up and return points:\nTrekking, gravel and electric bicycles are available. The operator says that the base package includes a repair kit and pump, lock, lights where needed and a water bottle; panniers, a handlebar bag, helmet and phone holder are extras. Daily luggage transfer between lodgings is not provided, but panniers or a trailer can be rented, and selected luggage-storage and transfer services are available.\nThree options are offered: about 400 km through southern Sweden followed by a ferry to Gdynia/Gda\u0144sk, about 600 km through Sweden, Bornholm and Sassnitz, and about 900 km through Gedser, Rostock and the German and Polish coast. The last is closest to southern EV10, but from Copenhagen to Gedser it follows EV7 and Danish route 9, joining EV10 only in Rostock. The stated rental duration is usually 7\u201312 days. Check current prices, bicycle availability and booking conditions at OneWayBikeTours \u2013 Copenhagen\u2013Gda\u0144sk.\nPractical maps, timetables and resources.\n&lt;maplink text=\"\" class=\"no-icon\" group=\"evbase\"&gt;{\"type\":\"Feature\",\"properties\":{\"title\":\"EV10 \u2013 Sweden \u2013 base route\",\"description\":\"Simplified national-section geometry from OSM relation 63584; retrieved: 2026-07-31\",\"stroke\":\"#F2C500\",\"stroke-width\":5,\"stroke-opacity\":0.82},\"geometry\":{\"type\":\"MultiLineString\",\"coordinates\":[12.99904,55.60931],[12.99805,55.60996],[12.99733,55.61246],[12.99229,55.61277],[12.98762,55.61224],[12.98592,55.61364],[12.98299,55.6177],[12.9822,55.61783],[12.9818,55.6202],[12.97744,55.61965],[12.97198,55.61505],[12.97278,55.61318],[12.97195,55.6125],[12.97263,55.61053],[12.97339,55.60989],[12.97478,55.61005],[12.97514,55.60976],[12.97503,55.60924],[12.97331,55.60894],[12.97355,55.60842],[12.97611,55.60748],[12.9787,55.60562],[12.95594,55.59903],[12.94381,55.59462],[12.93796,55.59152],[12.94147,55.5902],[12.94061,55.58962],[12.93426,55.5868],[12.93001,55.586],[12.92755,55.58696],[12.92537,55.58507],[12.91909,55.58139],[12.91481,55.57737],[12.913,55.57739],[12.90522,55.57348],[12.9042,55.57236],[12.90692,55.57208],[12.90772,55.57009],[12.89999,55.57038],[12.89672,55.569],[12.89722,55.56798],[12.8989,55.56732],[12.89825,55.56686],[12.89688,55.56639],[12.89308,55.56641],[12.89112,55.56484],[12.89106,55.56404],[12.89305,55.5637],[12.8969,55.56398],[12.90017,55.56323],[12.90575,55.56309],[12.91026,55.56239],[12.91022,55.56193],[12.90863,55.56199],[12.90809,55.56095],[12.90843,55.55079],[12.90886,55.55022],[12.91712,55.55048],[12.91953,55.54021]